WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:07.259
From the medieval knights of Europe, in full
plate armour, to the silent ninja-assassins

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:08.660
of Japan.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:14.420
Which warrior culture from history, were the
fastest, deadliest and most adept at killing?

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.670
Who will take the crown?

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.440
Let's find out.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.310
Aztecs

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.170
First up is the ancient Mexican civilisation
of the Aztecs.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.090
War was such an integral part of Aztec culture.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:35.300
That when a new Aztec leader was elected it
was expected of him to immediately wage a

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.550
military campaign against an enemy tribe to
prove his worth.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.680
When Aztecs attacked an enemy they had two
goals, firstly to take their land and make

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:51.510
it theirs and secondly to take prisoners so
they could sacrifice them to the gods.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.579
Making the Aztec warriors a force to be feared,
because unlike most fighting forces that will

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.680
give you a clean death the Aztecs were a lot
more brutish when it came to disposing of

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.970
their enemies.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:08.060
Prisoners of war would often be strangled
or stoned to death during religious ceremonies.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.750
They were masters of fear and intimidation.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.690
In fact they designed a special musical instrument
that had the sole purpose of intimidating

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.670
the enemy before a battle.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:24.070
It was called the Aztec death whistle and
it was in the shape of a skull; it produced

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.510
a truly horrific sound.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:30.590
This is the noise it made when you blew into
it.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:38.750
That's just one whistle.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.850
Now imagine a thousand Aztec warriors charging
towards you whilst blowing on a thousand death

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.909
whistles in a bone-chilling symphony.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:49.520
I don't know about you but I'd be off.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.520
Mongols

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.220
The Mongols were an Asian army led by the
revered Genghis Khan.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:57.350
They were focused on one goal - destruction.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.230
They destroyed and conquered everything in
their paths.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:05.090
They took no prisoners and were widely considered
as a bunch of barbarians and savages.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:10.009
Their combat skills however, have been matched
by few throughout history.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:13.189
They fought on horseback and were masters
of the bow and arrow.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:18.379
They specialised in shooting arrows whilst
riding their horses at high speeds, and they

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:19.769
were bloody good at it.

00:02:19.769 --> 00:02:24.109
They used a variety of different bows and
arrows, such as the composite bow which specialised

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:25.700
in ripping through armour.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.769
They also used their so called "howling" arrows
that would emit a terrifying sound whilst

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:35.689
flying through the air, this sound would disorientate
the enemy and cause panic.

00:02:35.689 --> 00:02:40.941
Their fearsome fighting prowess allowed Genghis
Khan and his Mongol army to conquer more of

00:02:40.941 --> 00:02:44.209
the world that any other empire in history.

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:45.209
Māori

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:48.480
The Māori are the indigenous people of New
Zealand.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.249
They were well known for eating their conquered
foes, because they believed they would gain

00:02:53.249 --> 00:02:54.249
their mana.

00:02:54.249 --> 00:02:56.550
Mana was at the core of the Māori's beliefs.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.150
Mana was believed to be spiritual power and
prestige.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.930
The Maori would intimidate their enemies by
performing a special dance before a fight

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:40.829
called the Haka Peruperu.

00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:45.669
The same dance is still performed today by
New Zealand's official rugby team, the All

00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:49.620
Blacks, before every game, to intimidate their
opponents.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.620
Ninjas

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:55.900
Next up are the masters of stealth, the silent
assassins known as Ninjas.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:01.579
They started off as humble farmers, but unsatisfied
with the way they were being treated by the

00:04:01.579 --> 00:04:02.699
samurai military.

00:04:02.699 --> 00:04:07.709
They trained rigorously in the shadows to
become silent, deadly killers and rose up

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:09.060
against the samurai.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.549
But, being poor farmers, they couldn't defeat
the samurai in open combat, because, unlike

00:04:14.549 --> 00:04:17.010
the samurai they had no armour.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:21.820
So they devised ways to be unseen and kill
the samurai when the least expected it, in

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.420
the most underhanded and devious ways.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:30.620
They were known for their superior ability
to kill and disappear in seconds.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.920
Owning weapons was illegal in Japan for anyone
expect the samurai military.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.400
So ninjas had to fashion their weapons out
of simple farming tools such as the sickle

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.320
- which they turned into the deadly kusarigama.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:48.840
They also used a short sword called a ninjatō,
similar to a Katana, but shorter.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.560
The ninjatō was lightweight and fast.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.600
They also had an arsenal of long range weapons
such as the poisonous blowgun, the deadly

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.090
shuriken, or ninja star.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:04.720
As well as black eggs which were egg shells
painted black and filled with ground up shards

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.720
of glass.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.130
Their purpose was to blind and disorientate
the enemy, ninjas would throw them into their

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:13.880
opponent's face, blinding them and causing
agonising pain.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.880
Persian Immortals

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.890
Next up is the Persian Immortals.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:20.330
They served as the imperial guard for the
Persian Empire.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:25.170
The immortals were a group of heavy infantry
that stood 10,000 strong.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:30.810
They got their name because they never seemed
to die, every time an immortal died, fell

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:36.480
ill, was injured or died in battle, they were
instantly replaced by another reserve immortal

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.280
- so there was always exactly 10,000.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:44.770
Also, if an immortal died during combat their
body would be immediately pulled from the

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:50.220
battle field by the other immortals, and replaced
by a new immortal from the reserves.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:54.880
This was done to maintain the impression that
they were un-killable, hence the name.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:58.980
They fought with shields and spears and also
used a bow and arrow from afar.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.730
They weren't particularly skilled with the
bow, but it didn't matter because they would

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:08.190
overwhelm their enemies by firing thousands
of arrows all in unison, leaving the enemy

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.520
with nowhere to hide.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.520
Roman Legion

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:15.190
Next up is the foundation of the Roman army,
the Roman legion.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:19.900
They were the infantry that helped to conquer
and create the most powerful empire in the

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.050
history of the world, the Roman Empire.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:28.720
The Roman Empire was large and wealthy and
the Roman legion, therefore, had the best

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.380
armour, swords, shields and spears that money
could buy.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:36.960
They went to the effort of covering themselves
in all that nice armour and then they wore

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.180
sandals, seriously.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:42.650
But sandals aside, they were masters of the
shield and spear combination.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:48.190
But what made the Roman legion and subsequently
the Roman empire so successful was the fact

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.700
that they were constantly adapting.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:55.190
As soon as they found fighting practices and
techniques that were better than their own,

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:59.670
they would instantly abandon their old ways
in favour of the new techniques.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:03.940
This enabled them to always stay ahead of
their enemies and hold the Roman empire for

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.650
over 500 years.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:11.460
In training they would focus on mastering
the thrust of a sword or spear, instead of

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.460
the slash.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:17.621
The thrust was far more lethal when facing
armoured opponents and meant the Roman legion

00:07:17.621 --> 00:07:20.580
had higher kill rates than their enemies during
battles.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:21.580
Samurai

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:27.070
Next up is a fearless band of warriors bound
by honour and duty, of course I'm talking

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.730
about the samurai.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:34.540
They mastered the sharpest sword that has
ever been forged, the legendary, the deadly,

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.540
katana.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:39.710
The katana could easily slice a man in half
in the right hands.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:43.470
Samurai were highly trained and incredibly
disciplined killing machines.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.900
They led their lives by the code of Bushido,
meaning the "way of the warrior".

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.840
But by far what made the samurai so unbelievably
deadly was that they weren't afraid to give

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.110
their lives for their masters.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:08:00.080
They were trained to believe that, before
all things, a samurai should constantly keep

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:05.880
in the forefront of his mind a simple, inevitable
truth that "they had to die".

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:11.400
And if they didn't achieve their goals or
their master's goals before dying it was considered

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.750
cowardly.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:18.370
Because of these beliefs, if a samurai failed
in battle they would commit ritual suicide,

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:22.350
often voluntarily, but sometimes as a punishment
from their masters.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:27.360
This ritual suicide was known as "seppuku",
and involved the Samurai stabbing himself

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:33.380
in his stomach with a short sword then dragging
the blade to the left or right to slice open

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.659
his abdomen and disembowel himself.

00:08:36.659 --> 00:08:40.719
That's pretty darn gruesome and it meant only
those with the strongest minds would become

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:42.719
samurai warriors.

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:47.019
This absence of a fear of death made the samurai
the most fearless warriors that ever lived.

00:08:47.019 --> 00:08:48.240
The Vikings

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:53.750
Next up, the most feared fighting force in
Europe between the 8th and 11th centuries,

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.470
the Vikings.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.110
Barbaric in nature, their attacks were fast
and brutal.

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:03.160
They effortlessly mowed down everyone who
dared get in their way.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.980
They raided and pillaged across almost all
of Europe, often grabbing what riches they

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.360
could before returning to their homeland of
Scandinavia.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.059
The battle-axe was the weapon of choice for
these nordic brutes, who were often large

00:09:16.059 --> 00:09:17.170
in size.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:22.320
Making them easily able to overpower their
skinny little south-western European counterparts.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.139
However, the rumours that they had horns on
their helmets and they drank out of the skulls

00:09:27.139 --> 00:09:29.770
of their enemies are complete myths.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.360
They were actually gentle giants.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.139
No, just kidding they were violent savages.

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:38.269
Even their religion was centred around war
and they believed that when a viking died

00:09:38.269 --> 00:09:43.899
they would go to Valhalla where they would
prepare for an enormous battle called Ragnarök.

00:09:43.899 --> 00:09:48.720
But they did do some good for Europe, they
were exceptionally good at trading with the

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.639
rest of Europe, so we also have a lot to thank
them for.

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:52.639
The Medieval Knight

00:09:52.639 --> 00:09:57.709
Next up is the medieval knight, a fully clad,
battle-hardened warrior that was a force to

00:09:57.709 --> 00:09:59.339
be reckoned with.

00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:04.029
Knights were the wealthiest and best trained
warriors in the entire medieval world.

00:10:04.029 --> 00:10:09.149
Often fighting on horseback with only the
best armour, shields and tempered steel long-swords.

00:10:09.149 --> 00:10:13.490
Knights trained their entire lives, mainly
because they were idolised and young boys

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:16.259
would often want to become knights from an
early age.

00:10:16.259 --> 00:10:20.220
They were the upholders of piece and fought
by a strict code of honour.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:25.209
All knights had to swear by the "Knights Code
of Chivalry" which included lines such as

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:31.300
"To protect the weak and defenceless", "To
fight for the welfare of all" and "Never to

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.529
refuse a challenge from an equal".

00:10:33.529 --> 00:10:38.709
That's right, knights were bound by law to
always accept a duel, even if they happened

00:10:38.709 --> 00:10:43.769
to be in the middle of taking a bath or some
other equally uncompromising situation.

00:10:43.769 --> 00:10:47.809
For this reason they had trusty squires who
would always be by their side to have their

00:10:47.809 --> 00:10:49.600
armour, sword and shield handy.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.600
Spartans

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:55.879
And lastly are, arguably, the most skilled
fighters to ever grace the ancient world,

00:10:55.879 --> 00:10:58.310
the legendary Spartans.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.939
Spartans underwent brutal training their entire
lives.

00:11:00.939 --> 00:11:06.050
At the tender age of seven Spartan boys were
ripped from their family home and began the

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:08.550
"Agoge" - the state-sponsored training programme.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:16.149
The Agoge was utterly relentless and violent,
which prepared them for real-life combat situations.

00:11:16.149 --> 00:11:20.600
Unlike almost every other warrior in history,
Spartans had no professions to distract them

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:24.790
from training, they were not smiths, bakers
or candlestick makers.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:30.819
They were one thing and one thing only: elite
fighting machines, trained to kill and not

00:11:30.819 --> 00:11:31.819
to be killed.

00:11:31.819 --> 00:11:36.579
When a child was born in Sparta the mother
would instantly bathe it in wine, to ensure

00:11:36.579 --> 00:11:37.579
it was strong.

00:11:37.579 --> 00:11:40.579
If the child was weak, it would die soon after.

00:11:40.579 --> 00:11:45.200
Later the elders would expect the baby, if
it was found to be deformed in any way the

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.709
poor thing was thrown from the top of a cliff
into a chasm.

00:11:48.709 --> 00:11:53.029
This horrifically brutal treatment produced
the greatest legion of close combat fighters

00:11:53.029 --> 00:11:55.040
the world has ever seen.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:59.970
They specialised in three main weapons: The
spear which could kill a man several feet

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:02.329
away, with a single trust.

00:12:02.329 --> 00:12:09.579
The short-sword and finally the most important
part of their arsenal, the round Spartan shield,

00:12:09.579 --> 00:12:13.230
which was used just as much offensively as
it was defensively.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:18.120
A spartan was covered in bronze from head
to toe, they were like tanks - tanks that

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.440
could stab things.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:24.610
The Spartans are best known for their heroic
performance at the Battle of Thermopylae in

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.839
480 BC.

00:12:26.839 --> 00:12:35.199
When just 300 spartans, led by King Leonidas
of Sparta, fought off 150,000 Persian soldiers

00:12:35.199 --> 00:12:37.749
for three days straight.

00:12:37.749 --> 00:12:43.260
The Spartans eventually lost the fight, but
their display of courage, resilience and amazing

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:49.470
fighting ability against an army that so greatly
outnumbered them, has never been matched in

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.350
all of history.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:56.570
For goodness sake there were 500 Persians
for each Spartan, and they lasted three days,

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.560
that's pretty damn impressive.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:02.870
The Spartans had a powerful saying that their
wives would tell them before leaving for battle,

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:06.420
"come back with the shield or on top of it."

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:12.009
Which meant, don't come back unless you are
victorious.

